{"title":"2007 iTest Problems/Ultimate Question","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The following questions are from the \"Ultimate Question\" of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest\" title=\"2007 iTest\">2007 iTest</a>, but with the T-values substituted.  This is for people who want to work on the problems without having to solve the previous problems.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_51\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 51</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_52\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 52</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_53\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 53</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_54\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 54</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_55\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 55</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_56\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 56</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_57\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 57</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_58\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 58</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_59\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 59</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_60\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 60</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_51\">Problem 51</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Ultimate_Question&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 51\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find the highest point (largest possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-coordinate) on the parabola\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/f/79fda67b1f2e64588c88901a47c2a1543516d336.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y=-2x^2+ 28x+ 418\\]\" width=\"174\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_51\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 51\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_52\">Problem 52</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Ultimate_Question&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 52\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the region consisting of points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> of the Cartesian plane satisfying both\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/3/c23276358504c5ad4145e2e241000562f6c3212f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x|-|y|\\le 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/7/b47a187a3ec0e8e2d9308d833b0042e39f3c4d28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|y|\\le 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. Find the area of region <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_52\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 52\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_53\">Problem 53</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Ultimate_Question&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 53\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Three distinct positive Fibonacci numbers, all greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/1/39136d22764e01756b25a97e28f5e6486bd509ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1536$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />, are in arithmetic progression. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the smallest possible value of their sum. Find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/d/b0db9f93bcba529c93ae151a1ac5c740eec7cca3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2007$\" width=\"36\" height=\"12\" />. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_53\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 53\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_54\">Problem 54</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Ultimate_Question&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 54\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Consider the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/1/3813192dd8313c44a55fac0d612dcec657756ab8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 2007)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />. Inserting the difference between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/d/b0db9f93bcba529c93ae151a1ac5c740eec7cca3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2007$\" width=\"36\" height=\"12\" /> between them, we get the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/0/b70e1dd54d6e9ada312b6649c942a9b3b1c1af24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 2006, 2007)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" />. Repeating the process of inserting differences between numbers, we get the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/3/1a3862aba739f7c2269901e02996d69d0a47af91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 2005, 2006, 1, 2007)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"172\" height=\"18\" />. A third iteration of this process results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/7/af773f45bfd6dee23d94e5f794a16f39f31167d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 2004, 2005, 1, 2006, 2005, 1, 2006, 2007)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"326\" height=\"20\" />. A total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/d/b0db9f93bcba529c93ae151a1ac5c740eec7cca3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2007$\" width=\"36\" height=\"12\" /> iterations produces a sequence with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/8/ff87bd1b14b30f3066127b94835ab76d09c6f124.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2007}+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"16\" /> terms. If the integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/a/90ae760d1ea10eb7a90d22087b3c7e2393d02117.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2004$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" /> appears a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> times among these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/8/ff87bd1b14b30f3066127b94835ab76d09c6f124.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2007}+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"16\" /> terms, find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> gets divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/d/b0db9f93bcba529c93ae151a1ac5c740eec7cca3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2007$\" width=\"36\" height=\"12\" />. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_54\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 54\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_55\">Problem 55</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Ultimate_Question&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 55\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/d/30dbc4564abd0941b18a812c8fceb5571d95c88a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R=675$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the smallest real solution of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/5/4f5b09754b1ba93e3c1568e8cc33e5e9e5d00fa9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x^2+Rx+R=90x\\sqrt{x+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"219\" height=\"18\" />. Find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/1/441416e660d25335f27e55334ac2a06e51541c97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"19\" />. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_55\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 55\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_56\">Problem 56</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Ultimate_Question&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 56\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>In the binary expansion of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/c/aecf4a438328354ca1fcc8c13bd1341a8f907fee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{2^{2007}-1}{2^{225}-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"74\" height=\"42\" />, how many of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/b/50b19142d92b7b4f1a115c4ec91766582e2b8faf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10,000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" /> digits to the right of the radix point are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />'s? \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_56\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 56\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_57\">Problem 57</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Ultimate_Question&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 57\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>How many positive integers are within <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/e/c1e8286b5c37bb9cdf7b53ea08a8625c5b2665a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$810$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> of exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/6/3e6ee3b4b4aeea098b78ff34ab5a2129e75eb544.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor \\sqrt{810} \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"55\" height=\"22\" /> perfect squares? (Note: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d1c4bc3de166b868140cd363c01ed76c442259c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0^2=0$\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" /> is considered a perfect square.) \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_57\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 57\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_58\">Problem 58</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Ultimate_Question&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 58\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For natural numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/4/f24c5767fd4a3d4b1cf770981fe45377fcf61f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k,n\\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" />, we define\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/7/a47d32ef7dbe4b05db19a8a472f8633b2db03705.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S(k,n)=\\left\\lfloor\\frac{2^{n+1}+1}{2^{n-1}+1}\\right\\rfloor+\\left\\lfloor\\frac{3^{n+1}+1}{3^{n-1}+1}\\right\\rfloor+\\cdots+\\left\\lfloor\\frac{k^{n+1}+1}{k^{n-1}+1}\\right\\rfloor\\]\" width=\"437\" height=\"43\" />\nCompute the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/2/f9215ddb0a76d20e6c4def31c95719f71c691cbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(10,112)-S(10,55)+S(10,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"255\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_58\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 58\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_59\">Problem 59</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Ultimate_Question&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 59\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Fermi and Feynman play the game <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/6/fa6363c7be7f86c6cd33ac1ac79780e84aaca06a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{Probabicloneme}$\" width=\"112\" height=\"12\" /> in which Fermi wins with probability <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/c/e0c22354f6f8870c3a024305aa3afed00b26bcf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a/b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are relatively prime positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/7/c57d4e5ba159e4d432e2429bcf40267921c3b372.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a/b&lt;1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />. The rest of the time Feynman wins (there are no ties or incomplete games). It takes a negligible amount of time for the two geniuses to play <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/6/fa6363c7be7f86c6cd33ac1ac79780e84aaca06a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{Probabicloneme}$\" width=\"112\" height=\"12\" /> so they play many many times. Assuming they can play infinitely many games (eh, they're in Physicist Heaven, we can bend the rules), the probability that they are ever tied in total wins after they start (they have the same positive win totals) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/5/62513873bdc00aca23b2b44da3e860979eaf81a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" />. Find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_59\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 59\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_60\">Problem 60</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Ultimate_Question&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 60\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/c/ddcf018b48cc5f089be6e8ff32db360d1bd69567.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=99$\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/a/9daa16454ec7795b0cedd0c25523bc91dc9caa3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=120$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"78\" height=\"13\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> bisects angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/d/2edcdc0d73ef64ec441f60a3a8dccdbd10aa61a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BAC$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />. The circle through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/bef747a48a2a8d43c4841e12c89f2de2502a672e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> has center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3216e8846eb44f1055c322fb5bd30169d5d62cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> and intersects line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> again at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c71f19552a05ee5e2b31e94aff3fb986884bf31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, and likewise the circle through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/a/faafcc2f53726bb09ac20d940deb797970210fc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> has center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/e/5ee48e5d3968014ef1e27c31e56d2f7ea5f8cb1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> and intersects line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> again at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b798193cb94562989018728e1151587c618655b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"16\" />. If the four points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/5/245b6c1d9b5a4104f3bab8caf1cbb7aa950ac676.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;, C&#39;, O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/e/5ee48e5d3968014ef1e27c31e56d2f7ea5f8cb1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> lie on a circle, find the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_60\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 60\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018053616\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.029 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.042 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 325/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 11368/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:16397:|#|:idhash:canon